## Trained on real UI gaze data, not natural scenes

Most open-source saliency models are trained on the [SALICON dataset](http://salicon.net/): natural photographs scraped from Flickr. Those models have learned to predict attention on photos of mountains and faces and street scenes. Put a web page in front of them and they produce a diffuse centrality blob. They don't know that "Start free trial" is the most important element on the screen; they see a rectangular region with text and mild contrast and model it accordingly.

